.TH NEWSCID 1 "October 2026" "NewScid 1.3.30" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
newscid \- Modern Chess Workstation and .si4 Information Database
.br
newscid-import \- High-speed standalone PGN & online incremental database importer
.br
newscid-fairplay \- Standalone longitudinal fair-play & time-control consistency analyzer
.br
newscid-scout \- Standalone opponent scouting dossier, opening exploiter & crosstable generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B newscid
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B newscid-import
\fB\-db\fR \fIDATABASE.si4\fR [\fB\-pgn\fR \fIFILE.pgn\fR] [\fB\-lichess\fR \fIUSER\fR] [\fB\-chesscom\fR \fIUSER\fR] [\fB\-max\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-dedup\fR] [\fB\-compact\fR]
.br
.B newscid-fairplay
\fB\-db\fR \fIDATABASE.si4\fR \fB\-player\fR \fINAME\fR [\fB\-max\fR \fI300\fR] [\fB\-json\fR]
.br
.B newscid-scout
\fB\-db\fR \fIDATABASE.si4\fR [\fB\-player\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-exploit-color\fR \fIwhite|black\fR] [\fB\-book-out\fR \fIFILE.bin\fR] [\fB\-crosstable\fR \fIEVENT\fR] [\fB\-json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B NewScid
is a Linux chess database and graphical analysis program written in Go and Vue 3.
It provides native reading and writing support for SCID v4 binary databases (\fB.si4\fR index, \fB.sg4\fR Huffman-compressed games, \fB.sn4\fR front-coded namebase tries), PGN/Zstandard streams, and UCI chess engine analysis.
.PP
All user documentation, contextual feature help (\fBF1\fR), and system manual pages (\fBman 1 newscid\fR) are stored locally on the system.
.PP
Alongside the main graphical application (\fBnewscid\fR), three standalone CLI utilities (\fBnewscid-import\fR, \fBnewscid-fairplay\fR, and \fBnewscid-scout\fR) are installed for batch database maintenance, statistical screening, and tournament preparation from the terminal.
.SH OPTIONS (newscid)
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Output version, git commit, build date, and runtime architecture, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-db " \fIPATH\fR"
Open the specified database (\fB.si4\fR or \fB.pgn\fR) upon startup.
.TP
.BR \-\-window\-panel " \fIPANEL_ID\fR"
Launch a dedicated multi-screen/Hyprland window rendering a specific detached workstation panel (\fBboard\fR, \fBtree\fR, \fBengine\fR, \fBgames\fR, \fBnotation\fR, \fBportal\fR, or \fBdb-roles\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-workspace " \fIID\fR"
Target compositor workspace when launching a detached screen panel window.
.SH COMPANION WORKSTATION CLI PROGRAMS
.SS newscid-import
Standalone high-speed PGN and online game importer, signature deduplicator, and physical compactor:
.TP
.BI \-db " PATH"
Target SCID database path (\fB.si4\fR). Created automatically if it does not exist.
.TP
.BI \-pgn " FILE"
Import games from a PGN file into the target database, skipping games whose 64-bit signature already exists.
.TP
.BI \-lichess " USERNAME"
Incrementally sync newest and historical backfill games from Lichess.org without recounting existing games.
.TP
.BI \-chesscom " USERNAME"
Incrementally sync newest and historical backfill games from Chess.com without recounting existing games.
.TP
.BI \-max " N"
Maximum number of new unimported online games to fetch (default: 250).
.TP
.B \-dedup
Run signature-based duplicate removal (default: true).
.TP
.B \-compact
Physically compact deleted records from the \fB.si4\fR/\fB.sg4\fR files after import.
.SS newscid-fairplay
Standalone longitudinal statistical fair-play and time-control consistency analyzer:
.TP
.BI \-db " PATH"
SCID database path (\fB.si4\fR) to inspect.
.TP
.BI \-player " NAME"
Player name or handle to evaluate across all matching games in the database.
.TP
.BI \-max " N"
Maximum number of games to analyze (default: 300).
.TP
.B \-json
Emit the full statistical dossier as formatted JSON instead of Markdown.
.SS newscid-scout
Standalone opponent scouting dossier, opening vulnerability exploiter, and crosstable utility:
.TP
.BI \-db " PATH"
SCID database path (\fB.si4\fR) to scan.
.TP
.BI \-player " NAME"
Opponent name for scouting dossier or opening vulnerability analysis.
.TP
.BI \-exploit-color " white|black"
Build an Anti-Persona opening exploit tree targeting the opponent's repertoire as White or Black.
.TP
.BI \-book-out " FILE.bin"
Compile and export the generated opening refutation lines to a binary Polyglot (\fB.bin\fR) opening book.
.TP
.BI \-crosstable " EVENT"
Calculate a Round-Robin or Swiss tournament crosstable with Sonneborn-Berger, Buchholz, and TPR for the specified event name.
.TP
.B \-json
Emit output as formatted JSON.
.SH WORKSPACES, DETACHABLE PANELS & PERSISTENT CONFIG
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAll Panels Relocatable & Detachable\fR: Every workstation panel—including the \fBChessboard\fR, \fBScorebook\fR, \fBUCI Engine & Coach\fR, \fBOpening Tree & Tablebase\fR, \fBDatabase Game Browser\fR, \fBEval Graph\fR, and \fBStudy/Filter\fR—can be docked Left, Right, or Bottom, reordered, hidden, or detached into a draggable floating window or dedicated Hyprland workspace window.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPersistent User Configuration\fR: Any change to panel docking/floating geometry, default startup database, reference database, board theme, piece set, UI theme, or notation style is immediately persisted to \fI~/.config/newscid/preferences.json\fR.
.SH WORKSTATION MODULES
.SS Native SCID Binary Database Engine, Search, Write Locking & Sub-DB Builder
Reads and writes 47-byte index records (\fB.si4\fR), Huffman-compressed move streams (\fB.sg4\fR), and front-coded namebase tries (\fB.sn4\fR).
Provides board position search (\fBMatch Board\fR), opening move-sequence and ECO range filtering, and a customizable \fBFamous Players\fR selector (Bobby Fischer, Magnus Carlsen, Garry Kasparov, Mikhail Tal, etc.) with automatic FIDE alias resolution.
Every database enforces a configurable write policy (\fBEditable\fR for personal/persona databases, \fBSync-Only\fR for imported reference databases, or \fBLocked\fR read-only) to prevent accidental edits.
Supports extracting sub-databases across multiple source \fB.si4\fR/\fB.pgn\fR databases and performing a \fBFactory Reset\fR (with optional \fB.tar.gz\fR backup).
.SS Player Personas & Incremental Online Synchronization
Unifies disparate database identifiers (FIDE OTB name, Chess.com username, Lichess handle) under a single Persona profile with its own dedicated \fB.si4\fR database. Syncing a player or persona fetches the newest games since the last sync first, then backfills older historical games while skipping games already present in the database.
.SS Longitudinal Fair-Play & Time-Control Consistency Inspector
Evaluates player move quality, Average Centipawn Loss (ACPL), top-move rank distribution, blunder rates, and consistency across Bullet, Blitz, Rapid, and Classical time controls using calibrated human baselines.
.SS Opponent Scouting & Anti-Persona Opening Exploiter
Generates pre-game scouting dossiers and scans an opponent's opening tree to identify statistically weak nodes where they score poorly, exporting Polyglot (\fB.bin\fR) opening books.
.SS Player Simulation Bot & Engine Sparring
Simulates any database player or Persona by playing their historical opening repertoire probabilistically and transitioning to a rating-calibrated UCI engine with tactical blunder protection. Both the board evaluation bar and the 6-pillar Positional & Material Imbalance bar report from an absolute White perspective (+ = White advantage, \- = Black advantage).
.SS Position Coach, Blunder Radar & 7-Piece Tablebases
Explains the strategic and tactical rationale behind moves, highlights undefended/hanging pieces via the Blunder Radar, and probes 7-piece Syzygy/Lichess endgame tablebases for exact WDL and DTZ.
.SS Cyclical Tactical Drill, Lichess Theme Radar & Cognitive Drills
Includes the \fBCyclical Tactical Drill & Theme Mastery\fR module—implementing cyclical puzzle-set repetition (similar to the training regimen popularized by GM Axel Smith and IM Hans Tikkanen's book "The Woodpecker Method") where puzzles extracted from the user's own game history are sorted from \fBEasy to Hard\fR and solved across repeated cycles with halved target times, alongside a 30+ theme Lichess-compatible tactical tagger and 9-axis Performance Radar chart (\fIRatingAvg \- 500 + 1000 * FirstWins / Attempts\fR). Also includes the Coordinate Speed Trainer (with 8x8 accuracy heatmap), Piece Safety Scanner, Intuition Evaluation Storm, Prophylaxis ("What Is Threatening?") Drill, Progressive Blindfold Tactics, Solitaire Chess (Guess the Move), Practical Repertoire Shortener, SM-2 Personal Blunder Vault, and \fB%clk\fR Time-Trouble & Clock-Management Dossier.
.SS Notation Styles & Game Publishing
Switches across 6 notation formats (\fBSAN\fR, \fBFAN\fR, \fBLAN\fR, \fBDescriptive\fR, \fBUCI\fR, \fBICCF\fR), provides a 16-NAG annotation palette, and exports annotated games to \fBLaTeX\fR, \fBHTML\fR, and \fBPDF\fR scorebooks.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
Open Local Manual & Contextual Help for the active dialog or workspace.
.TP
.B F2
Toggle live UCI engine analysis.
.TP
.B F3
Open Opening Tree & Polyglot Book Explorer.
.TP
.B F6
Open ECO Opening Classification Browser.
.TP
.B F7
Open Tournament Crosstables & Standings dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+1 .. Ctrl+4
Switch between Database, Analysis, Training, and Opening Prep workspaces.
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Open Universal Command Palette.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Open Workstation Preferences & Multi-Screen Panel Configuration.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O / Ctrl+N / Ctrl+S
Open database / New game / Save current game.
.TP
.B Ctrl+M
Open Database Maintenance, Compaction & Sorting dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
Open Header, Position, Opening, Material & Pawn-Structure Search dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Open Setup Board / FEN Editor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Space
Toggle Trial Mode (sandbox variation testing).
.TP
.B F / Space / Z
Flip board orientation / Toggle autoplay / Toggle Zen Mode.
.TP
.B ?
Display Keyboard Shortcuts reference.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/newscid/preferences.json
Persistent workstation panel layout, floating geometry, default database, database write policies, custom famous players, and visual theme configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/newscid/personas.json
Saved multi-alias Player Personas and sync metadata.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/newscid/databases/
Managed directory for user and focused SCID databases (\fB.si4\fR, \fB.sg4\fR, \fB.sn4\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/newscid/engines/
Managed directory for copied UCI chess engine binaries.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/newscid/books/opening/
Managed directory for copied Polyglot (\fB.bin\fR) opening books.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/newscid/books/endgame/
Managed directory for copied Syzygy (\fB.rtbw\fR/\fB.rtbz\fR) endgame tablebases.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/newscid/backups/
Opt-in compressed (\fB.tar.gz\fR) archives created prior to Factory Reset.
